    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.align\n\n### Description\n\nI'm trying to align inline comments in a few Lua lines; something like this:\r\n```lua\r\none = 'one' -- one\r\ntwo = 'two-2' -- two\r\nthree = '3' -- three\r\n```\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8.3\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Select the 3 lines in visual mode\r\n2. Go to interactive align mode\r\n3. Type `s` to enter \"split\"\r\n4. Type `--` and press `enter`\r\n5. I get the error\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI expect `--` to be treated as any other expression\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nI get the following error:\r\n\r\n```\r\nE5108: Error executing lua (mini.align) Pattern \"--\" can not advance search.\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        [C]: in function 'error'\r\n        ...vim/my_lazy/data/nvim/lazy/mini.align/lua/mini/align.lua:1940: in function 'error'\r\n        ...vim/my_lazy/data/nvim/lazy/mini.align/lua/mini/align.lua:1497: in function <...vim/my_lazy/data/n\r\nvim/lazy/mini.align/lua/mini/align.lua:1466>\r\n        vim/shared.lua: in function 'tbl_map'\r\n        ...vim/my_lazy/data/nvim/lazy/mini.align/lua/mini/align.lua:1459: in function 'action'\r\n        ...vim/my_lazy/data/nvim/lazy/mini.align/lua/mini/align.lua:1413: in function 'apply_step'\r\n        ...vim/my_lazy/data/nvim/lazy/mini.align/lua/mini/align.lua:672: in function 'align_strings'\r\n        ...vim/my_lazy/data/nvim/lazy/mini.align/lua/mini/align.lua:1657: in function 'process_current_regio\r\nn'\r\n        ...vim/my_lazy/data/nvim/lazy/mini.align/lua/mini/align.lua:775: in function 'align_user'\r\n        ...vim/my_lazy/data/nvim/lazy/mini.align/lua/mini/align.lua:813: in function 'action_visual'\r\n```",
