            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "To use \"as is\", you need to escape it. So type `%-%-`.\r\n\r\nAfter typing `s`, it [expects Lua pattern](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/8e007cf3ae8db59bd926a9fbaf7f0d25a7fe67ca/doc/mini-align.txt#L21). The `-` character has a [special meaning](https://www.lua.org/manual/5.1/manual.html#5.4.1) - it is a non-greedy version of `*` quantifier (like `a-`will match 0 or more shortest possible matches).",
