            "body": "> > With \"mini\" display in 'noice.nvim' they always appeared in right bottom side of screen\r\n> \r\n> Oh wait, what do you mean by this? Is there an additional setting that I missed? Because for me, they appear in the top right (similar to other \"notifications\" but they're just \"sticky\" and stay there)\r\n\r\nIn your case they come from [rcarriga/nvim-notify](https://github.com/rcarriga/nvim-notify). I tested with minimal dependencies without it, in which case [`mini` view](https://github.com/folke/noice.nvim#-views) is used (as per [documentation](https://github.com/folke/noice.nvim#-installation)). To force it for a particular part of config, I think you should use `view = 'mini'` inside its configuration table. Something like this, maybe:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('noice').setup({\r\n  messages = { view = 'mini' },\r\n})\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2023-02-03T15:33:04Z",
